{title: 036 - O Thou in Whose Presence}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #036 • BELOVED • 20.19}
{lyricist: Joseph Swain}
{composer: Freeman Lewis}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 36}
{meta: tune BELOVED}
{meta: meter 20.19}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C/E]O Thou in whose [G7]presence [C]my soul [Dm/A]takes [G]delight, [C/E]On whom in affliction [G]I [F#m]call,
[G]My [C/G]comfort [F/C]by [C]day and my [F/C]song [C]in the night, My hope, my salvation, [G]my [Dm/F]all!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C/E]His voice, as the sound of [Dm/F]the [C]dulcimer [F#m]sweet,
[C/E]Is heard through the [G]shadows [C/G]of [G]death;
[G]The [C/G]cedars of [F/C]Lebanon [C]bow at His [Dm/F]feet,
[G]The [C/G]air is [F/C]perfumed [C]with His [G]breath.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C/E]His lips, as a fountain [Dm/F]of [C]righteousness [F#m]flow,
[C/E]To water the [G]gardens [C/G]of [G]grace;
[G]From [C/G]which [F/C]their [C/G]salvation [G]the [C/G]Gentiles shall [Dm/F]know,
[G]And [C/G]bask in [F/C]the [C/G]smiles of His [G]face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C/E]He looks, and ten thousands [Dm/F]of [C]angels rejoice,
[C/E]And myriads wait for His [G]word;
[G]He [C/G]speaks, [F/C]and [C/G]eternity, filled with His [Dm/F]voice,
[G]Re-echoes [C]the praise of the [G]Lord.
{end_of_verse}
